title: Rhythm notes
intro: Notes from a chart scroll down lanes in time with the music, and every press is judged by the beat the player hears: Perfect, Great, Good or Miss.
project: Empty | Note Lanes

chapter: Lanes and a song | Entity > Genres > Rhythm > Note Lanes
say: A rhythm game is notes on the beat, lanes to bring them in, and a judgment for every press.
create: Note Lanes
expectcomponents: Note Lanes = Transform, BeatClock, NoteLanes
explain: component:NoteLanes | Note Lanes | Note Lanes come with four lanes, a beat clock, a song made in Griff, and a chart for it at three difficulties.
explain: field:NoteLanes.Song | Its song | The song picks its chart by name: Groove dot wav plays the Groove table.
expectvalue: Note Lanes.NoteLanes.Song = Music/Groove.wav
set: NoteLanes.Difficulty = Easy
explain: field:NoteLanes.Difficulty | Difficulty | Each note says which difficulties it's in, so one chart holds Easy, Normal and Hard.
expectvalue: Note Lanes.NoteLanes.Difficulty = Easy
explain: field:NoteLanes.PerfectWindow | Judging | A press within forty five milliseconds of the beat is Perfect, then Great, Good, or a Miss. The beat is the one the player hears, their audio offset allowed for.
explain: field:NoteLanes.Actions | Keys, buttons and fingers | D, F, J and K press the lanes, or the arrows, a controller, a click, or on a touch screen several fingers at once, for chords and holds.

chapter: The chart is a table | Data > Open Table
menu: Data > Open Table > Groove
expecttable: 208 rows, 4 columns
explain: panel:Tables | A row a note | A chart is a table: each note's beat, its lane, how many beats to hold it, and the difficulties it's in. It's a line a note in git, and a spreadsheet or formulas can write it.

chapter: Play | Play
play
wait: 3
expectvalue: Note Lanes.NoteLanes.IsPlaying = true
explain: game | Notes on the beat | The notes scroll down to the line in time with the music. Each press is judged and pops up, and the score, combo and accuracy are outputs anything can show.
tap: D
wait: 1.5
say: Every hit and miss sends a message too, so a note on the beat can fire a weapon or a miss can hurt the hero, in any genre. In a network game each player's own machine judges their presses, and the host adds up their score.
stop
